            <ArticleTitle>Pseudoaneurysm following high lateral myocardial infarction: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>210-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Male patient with a history of high lateral myocardial infarction experienced 45 days before admission was accepted to our clinic with the initial diagnosis of congestive heart failure. Physical examination revealed 2-3 degrees/6 systolic murmur in the mesocardiac region. Telecardiography revealed a mass of 12 x 6 cms in the left hilus. Pseudoaneurysm was diagnosed by transthoracic echocardiography and followed by left ventriculography. The symptoms of heart failure disappeared after successful surgical repair.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
